    <bpmn:userTask id="discover" name="Reads Discover">
      <bpmn:documentation>A plain arrival, on a phone or a desktop, opens on a page in front of the map: the map as one card, then new lists, the most opened places, a Play card offering lists to go round, swiped through one at a time with the reader's own walks first, popular lists and what is new on the map. Open map, a place on a shelf, the Places pill or an answer from the find bar leaves it for the map, and Back returns to it. A link about something — a place, a list, a chip — skips it. On a desktop the same shelves stand in another order — new lists, new on the map, overlooked places, popular lists — four lists at a time with arrows to the next four, and with no Play card and no Places pill. The round button at the end of the find bar opens More from here — the account, Ask, the flashcards, the colour, feedback and privacy — since the rail is put away.
when: discover_map
when: discover_list
when: discover_place
when: discover_play
when: discover_play_more
when: discover_lists_more
when: discover_all
ref: index.html #find-me
ref: assets/discover.js
ref: assets/app.js mountDiscover()
ref: functions/api/discover.js GET
ref: index.html #discover</bpmn:documentation>
